.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt SOJADB 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sojadb
.Nd manage the database of the soja IRC bouncer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm create-user
.Ar username
.Op Fl admin
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm change-password
.Ar username
.Sh DESCRIPTION
sojadb creates users and changes their passwords directly in the database that \fBsoja\fP(1) uses: the one named by the \fIdb\fP directive of the configuration file.
It is how the first (administrator) user is made, before soja has anyone to log in.
.Pp
The password is asked for on the terminal, without echo.
If standard input is not a terminal, one line is read from it as the password (and a warning is printed); an empty password is refused.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy "-h, -help"
.Pp
Show help message and quit.
.It Sy -config Ar path
.Pp
Path to the config file (default: /etc/soju/config).
.El
.Sh ACTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy create-user Ar username Op Ar -admin
.Pp
Create a new user, asking for the password.
With \fB-admin\fP the user is an administrator, who can create and change other users through BouncerServ (see \fBsoja\fP(1)).
.It Sy change-password Ar username
.Pp
Change the password of an existing user, asking for the new one.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr soja 1 ,
.Xr sojactl 1
.Sh AUTHORS
soja is a translation of soju, which is maintained by
.An Simon Ser Aq Mt contact@emersion.fr
and other open-source contributors.
soju's database tool is called sojudb.
